To see the output of the decorators in action, you can run a NAME_1 development server and visit the URL of the view with the decorator applied. For example, if you have a view with the `@login_required` decorator applied, you will need to log in before you can access the view. If you try to access the view without logging in, you will receive a 401 HTTP error response.

Here is an example of a JavaScript function that takes a JSON array of objects and turns it into an HTML table:
```
function jsonToTable(json) {
  var table = "<table>";
  for (var i = 0; i < json.length; i++) {
    var row = "<tr>";
    for (var key in json[i]) {
      row += "<td>" + json[i][key] + "</td>";
    }
    table += row + "</tr>";
  }
  table += "</table>";
  return table;
}
